  "result": "I fixed the bug: `IntRange` with `clamp=True` returned a value outside the range when a bound was open (`min_open` or `max_open`).\n\n**Cause:** In `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py:754`), an open bound was handled with `bound - dir`, which moves the value away from the range instead of into it. For example, `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-3` into `-1`, which isn't allowed. Closed bounds were not affected.\n\n**Fix:** I changed it to `bound + dir`, so an out-of-range value now lands on the nearest allowed integer. With `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, max_open=True, clamp=True)`, `-3` becomes `1`, `10` becomes `4`, and `3` stays `3`.\n\n**Tests:** I added two regression cases for clamping with open bounds to `tests/test_types.py`. The full test suite passes: 1908 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, none failed.\n\n`FloatRange` isn't affected, because it already refuses to combine open bounds with `clamp`.",
